questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot microservice running on Java 21 experiences severe performance degradation and high request latency under load. Monitoring shows carrier thread starvation in the JVM's `ForkJoinPool`. The team recently enabled Virtual Threads. You locate the following service method called during every HTTP request:

java
@Service
public class PaymentProcessingService {

    @Autowired
    private AuditLogger auditLogger;

    public void processPayment(PaymentRequest request) {
        synchronized (this) {
            auditLogger.logPaymentStart(request);
            byte[] signature = signPayloadRemote(request.getPayload()); // Remote HTTP REST Call
            auditLogger.logPaymentEnd(request, signature);
        }
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an asynchronous order processing pipeline loses tenant context and database transactions unexpectedly. The service method uses `CompletableFuture` within a Spring managed `@Transactional` method:

java
@Service
public class OrderService {

    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        orderRepository.save(order);

        CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            // Database read requiring active transaction context
            return orderRepository.findById(order.getId()).orElseThrow();
        }).thenAccept(updatedOrder -> {
            sendNotification(updatedOrder);
        });
    }
}


During execution, `orderRepository.findById(...)` fails with `TransactionRequiredException` or yields stale data because the context is missing.
